Let me now think about the design concretely.

### ratatui Rect hierarchy question

Ratatui does NOT have a hierarchy of Rect types. `Rect` is a plain `struct Rect { x: u16, y: u16, width: u16, height: u16 }`. There's no parent/child linkage. You can compute sub-Rects and nest widgets, but you manage that yourself. Ratatui does have `Rect::inner(padding)` which returns a sub-Rect inset by border width, and `Rect::intersection`, etc. So the answer: no hierarchy of types, but you can nest Rects manually — which is what the Layout already does.

Important nuance: When you render a widget (like a Block) into a Rect, ratatui draws within that Rect and the widget's own border occupies cells. If you render a Paragraph into the inner area of a Block, they're independent widgets in the same Frame; ratatui composes them. There's no automatic "this widget is a child of that Rect" binding — you pass the sub-Rect explicitly.

So the "paint a sub-block within the transcript" idea: yes, you can compute a sub-Rect (e.g., reserve the rightmost column for the scrollbar gutter) and render the scrollbar into that sub-Rect, and the paragraph into the remaining area. This is exactly what the current code does with `bar_area = Rect::new(area.right() - 1, ...)`. But note: currently the scrollbar is drawn on top of the border column (right border), not overlapping text, because the paragraph content fills columns 1..=right-2.

Actually wait — currently the transcript has `Borders::ALL`. The block border is 1 col on each side. Content area is `width - 2` (columns 1..right-2). The scrollbar gutter is the rightmost column (right border, column `right-1`). So scrollbar rides the right border column.

If we change to `Borders::TOP` only, then:
- Top border: 1 row.
- Content area: full width (no side borders), columns 0..right.
- Scrollbar gutter: we need to reserve the rightmost column so it doesn't overlap text. So content becomes columns 0..right-1, scrollbar at column right-1.

This is the key change: when we remove side borders, the transcript's `content_width` must change from `width - 2` to `width - 1` (one column reserved for the scrollbar gutter). And the padding (`full_width_line`) fills to `width - 1`.

