For drawing widgets inside a frame at a specific area, you just call `f.render_widget(widget, area)` where `area: Rect`. The frame doesn't need to own the area; multiple `render_widget` calls with overlapping `Rect`s all work. There's no "hierarchy" in the sense the user imagines — `Rect` is just a value type (x, y, width, height), and the frame's `render_widget` takes any Rect. So "using a sub-block" just means computing a Rect and calling render_widget on it.

